id|category|purpose|mechanism|experiment|production
acp-code|agents|Coordinate a research drafter and verifier implemented with different agent frameworks.|An ACP client sends work to separate CrewAI and Smolagents servers; their message contract matters more than framework choice.|Drop the verifier response and test deadline propagation, retry identity and whether an unverified draft can escape.|Run each agent as a separately authorized service; persist task IDs and message versions so retries cannot duplicate work.
agent-with-mcp-memory|memory|Give a local agent web tools, persistent graph memory and traceable behavior.|CrewAI uses MCP tools, Linkup search and Opik instrumentation; tool transport and memory semantics are separate concerns.|Ask a follow-up after restarting the client, then delete the remembered fact and verify that retrieval stops returning it.|Separate graph storage from stateless agent workers and enforce user-scoped memory reads, writes and deletion.
agent2agent-demo|agents|Understand agent-to-agent communication through sine, cosine and tangent services.|Three python_a2a agents expose mathematical tools; the useful lesson is discovery, message routing and task responses.|Exercise missing fields, nonnumeric arguments and tangent near a cosine zero; compare protocol errors with arithmetic errors.|Use typed capability contracts and bounded calls; production discovery must authenticate the advertised agent endpoint.
agentic_rag|rag|Route questions to document retrieval and use web fallback when needed.|CrewAI retrieval and response-synthesis agents wrap document tools; local DeepSeek and Llama variants show model substitution.|Build questions answered by documents, by the web only and by neither; measure fallback correctness separately from answer fluency.|Split ingestion from query serving, persist the vector index and attach source IDs to the final synthesis.
agentic_rag_deepseek|rag|Combine a local reasoning model with managed document parsing and search.|A custom CrewAI DocumentSearchTool delegates parsing and retrieval to GroundX before DeepSeek synthesizes the response.|Compare table-heavy pages against plain-text pages and verify the answer cites the exact supporting page.|Treat GroundX as an external data processor; track bucket ownership, ingestion state and document deletion across tenants.
ai-avatar-demo|memory|Supply a conversational avatar with a memory-aware AI backend.|FastAPI backend services combine streamed LLM completion, Zep context and Anam session tokens; visual avatar rendering is excluded.|Restart a session and verify context continuity, then test that a different user cannot retrieve the first user's facts.|Keep avatar session tokens short-lived; separate streaming API capacity from memory retrieval and external avatar transport.
ai-podcast-generation|media|Turn source material into a two-speaker podcast with cloud or local generation.|Separate scraping, script generation and Kokoro speech modules make the pipeline reusable without the Streamlit shell.|Hold the article constant and compare factual coverage, repeated claims and pronunciation between local and hosted generation.|Queue script and speech jobs independently; checkpoint each audio segment in object storage so a failed segment can be retried.
ai-podcast-generator|media|Create article-to-podcast audio using MiniMax generation and speech.|WebScraper, ScriptGenerator and TTSConverter isolate the source, dialogue and audio stages; the upstream presentation script is malformed.|Force a TTS segment failure and verify that the final manifest identifies missing segments instead of silently publishing partial audio.|Persist a script version and per-segment checksum; use an idempotent merge worker and bounded vendor polling.
ai_news_generator|agents|Generate sourced AI news using CrewAI and Cohere.|A small agent workflow gathers search results and synthesizes a news response; the original app mixes this logic with presentation.|Compare generated claims to retrieved URLs and score fabricated stories, duplicate coverage and publication-date errors.|Run collection as a scheduled job and require editorial acceptance before content reaches a publishing integration.
amazon-product-analysis-server|mcp|Expose product research and comparison through an MCP server.|TypeScript MCP resources call Bright Data tools and structure product results; interactive components are excluded.|Feed products with missing prices, multiple currencies and sponsored listings and check normalized provenance.|Cache source snapshots with capture times, cap scraping concurrency and isolate product retrieval credentials from MCP clients.
art_mcp_rl|training|Train an LLM to use MCP database tools with reinforcement learning.|ART rollouts call an MCP SQLite server and assign rewards to tool-assisted answers; training quality depends on the reward contract.|Construct a shortcut that earns reward without solving the query, then revise the grader and compare held-out task success.|Run rollouts against disposable read-only database snapshots; keep the training coordinator separate from inference and tool servers.
audio-analysis-toolkit|voice|Transcribe audio and expose summaries, speakers and analysis via MCP.|AssemblyAI processing is wrapped by server tools that return analysis artifacts; UI formatting is outside the AI workflow.|Compare overlapping speech, music and long pauses; score transcription errors and speaker assignment independently.|Use asynchronous transcription jobs, authenticated object URLs and explicit audio/transcript retention policies.
autogen-stock-analyst|agents|Use AutoGen with a custom model client for financial analysis and code generation.|CustomModelClient adapts a Qualcomm-hosted model to AutoGen's response, usage and cost interface.|Return a malformed provider response and compare behavior with a valid completion; test generated analysis against fixed market data.|Treat generated code as untrusted, execute it in a disposable sandbox and version the market-data snapshot used in the report.
biotech-agentic-analyst|structured|Extract scientific figures and produce structured research intelligence.|Mistral document extraction feeds a quality-routed CrewAI ScienceFlow and typed FigureIntelligence records.|Hide figure captions and compare biological claims with and without context; label unsupported quantitative conclusions.|Separate document parsing from analysis, retain page/figure provenance and require specialist review for consequential scientific use.
book-writer-flow|agents|Generate a researched outline and chapters with a persistent workflow state.|BookFlow produces an Outline, dispatches chapter-writing work and saves the assembled manuscript.|Interrupt after half the chapters, resume and check chapter identity, duplicated sections and citation consistency.|Persist chapter jobs independently, cap parallel model calls and keep publishing behind an explicit editorial step.
brand-monitoring|agents|Collect brand signals across multiple platforms and synthesize reports.|CrewAI flow dispatches platform-specific crews and combines their structured analyses.|Use duplicated posts across platforms and conflicting sentiment; score deduplication and source attribution.|Schedule source-specific ingestion with per-platform rate limits, then aggregate from immutable snapshots with freshness labels.
build-code-harness|agents|Study a coding-agent harness with planning, tools, checkpoints and approval.|The harness gives a model repository tools and a test runner; the bundled bank-account task is deliberately buggy learning material.|Run the account tests before and after an agent patch and inspect whether the agent weakens tests to claim success.|Run the harness in an ephemeral container without host credentials, limit write paths and retain patch/test evidence for review.
Build-reasoning-model|training|Train a reasoning-oriented model with GRPO and explicit answer-format rewards.|Unsloth and TRL generate grouped completions and combine correctness, integer-answer and XML-format reward functions.|Compare correctness-only rewards with combined formatting rewards and test whether syntactic compliance improves actual answer accuracy.|Use a dedicated GPU batch job, version reward code and datasets, and promote adapters only after independent evaluation.
chat-with-audios|rag|Retrieve answers from transcribed audio with document-style RAG.|Transcribe creates text, EmbedData stores vectors in Qdrant, and Retriever/RAG build a grounded answer.|Create questions whose evidence occurs at different timestamps and evaluate whether the retrieved transcript preserves those timestamps.|Persist transcript-to-audio provenance, avoid retranscribing unchanged audio and separate ASR capacity from query latency.
chat-with-code|rag|Retrieve repository context for code questions and validate responses.|The notebook ingests repository files, builds a LlamaIndex index and uses Qwen3-Coder with validation helpers.|Change one function in a pinned repository snapshot and measure whether stale index content leaks into answers.|Index allowlisted file types from pinned commits, strip secrets and attach file/line references to every supporting snippet.
code-model-comparison|evaluation|Compare code-generation models on a common repository context.|model_service performs parallel model calls, code_ingestion supplies context and Opik-based evaluation scores outputs.|Reverse candidate order, anonymize names and run executable correctness checks alongside judge scores.|Use a versioned benchmark runner with identical context budgets and record provider latency, token usage and model revision.
colbert-rag|retrieval|Understand late interaction through ColBERT-style MaxSim scoring.|Each query token takes its maximum dot product across document tokens; summing those maxima ranks documents.|Add zero padding to an all-negative document and show why unmasked padding can change the ranking.|Use masked token vectors, validate dimensions and measure the cost/recall tradeoff between candidate generation and reranking.
Colivara-deepseek-website-RAG|rag|Retrieve visually represented web pages and answer with a multimodal model.|Website screenshots become page-like documents; ColiVara search selects visual context for Janus-Pro synthesis.|Ask questions about a chart whose labels disappear in text extraction and compare visual and text retrieval.|Store screenshot provenance and crawl timestamps; isolate screenshot rendering workers from model-serving workers.
content_planner_flow|agents|Plan social content from web material and schedule a draft.|CrewAI Flow moves through scraping, platform-specific draft creation, plan saving and Typefully scheduling.|Replay the same publish event twice and verify that one accepted draft produces at most one external post.|Separate generation from publishing; persist a draft ID, explicit approval and an idempotency key for the scheduler.
context-engineering-pipeline|memory|Assemble useful context from documents, memory and structured stores under a token budget.|The notebook combines retrieval and memory search, estimates token use and summarizes blocks to fit the prompt.|Lower the context budget gradually and measure evidence retention, answer correctness and summary distortion.|Version context-selection policies and log selected source IDs plus token counts without logging private document contents.
context-engineering-workflow|memory|Coordinate multi-source research with parsing, retrieval and long-term context.|TensorLake document parsing, Voyage embeddings, Milvus retrieval and Zep memory feed CrewAI research tasks.|Remove one context source at a time and measure the effect on citations, stale facts and follow-up resolution.|Use separate ingestion and serving workers, request-scoped context assembly and independently scoped memory/vector stores.
conversational-support-flow|agents|Route support turns among order lookup, policy retrieval and live research.|CrewAI conversational routing persists session context; order lookup is deterministic while policy and research use agents.|Try another customer's known order ID and verify ownership before presenting tracking details; test pronoun follow-ups.|Add customer-scoped order access in the service boundary and persist session state in a shared store for multiple replicas.
corrective-rag|rag|Detect weak document evidence and recover through web search.|A LlamaIndex workflow retrieves, grades relevance, optionally searches the web and synthesizes a response.|Use misleading near-match chunks to measure when the relevance grader incorrectly accepts unsupported context.|Give each correction cycle a maximum count and token budget; record the reason for fallback and the resulting sources.
cursor_linkup_mcp|mcp|Expose deep web search and document retrieval to an MCP client.|server.py wraps Linkup search and a LlamaIndex RAGWorkflow as typed tools.|Call retrieval before ingestion and simulate a search timeout; tool responses should distinguish missing state from empty evidence.|Authenticate the MCP transport, isolate indexes by caller and make tool failures structured and retry-aware.
database-memory-agent|memory|Combine conversation history, semantic document search and tool selection in MongoDB.|Voyage embeddings support Atlas vector search; OpenAI chooses tools and generates responses using stored session history.|Use the same question in two sessions with different private documents and test for memory and vector-search leakage.|Filter on authenticated tenant/session IDs in every database query and manage vector-index dimension/version changes explicitly.
