document-chat-rag|rag|Build document-grounded question answering with local models and optional vector storage.|Notebook variants demonstrate index construction, local generation and retrieval/reranking choices.|Make a question with no supporting document and score abstention separately from plausible hallucination.|Use content-hashed ingestion, document-level ACLs and an explicit citation contract before adding API concurrency.
documentation-writer-flow|agents|Produce repository documentation through planning and writing agents.|A workflow clones code, produces a documentation plan and dispatches writing tasks; MCP exposes the process as a tool.|Ask it to document a function whose behavior differs from its name and verify that the generated explanation follows code.|Clone pinned revisions into disposable workspaces, write artifacts outside source and require review before publishing changes.
eval-and-observability|evaluation|Build an end-to-end RAG evaluation and trace collection pipeline.|Dataset-generation and application notebooks connect RAG calls to Opik and judge metrics.|Keep generated evaluation questions separate from a human-authored holdout and measure judge disagreement.|Run evaluation as a release job and sample redacted production traces with a retention limit and stable trace IDs.
eyelevel-mcp-rag|mcp|Expose complex-document ingestion and retrieval through GroundX-backed MCP tools.|The server provides document ingestion and search functions rather than a complete standalone chat application.|Search immediately after ingestion and verify that pending processing is distinct from a relevant-document miss.|Track ingestion jobs and tenant bucket IDs server-side; bound polling and prevent arbitrary access to shared buckets.
